# Bitdefender GravityZone API key, generated in Control Center -> My Account
# -> API keys. The key must have the Network, Policies, Reports, and
# Incidents APIs selected at generation time (see README's Authentication
# section) - Bitdefender's own key-generation UI only gates access at the
# API-area level, not per-method, so this connector's read-only posture is
# enforced entirely by its own code (see README's Scope section).
BITDEFENDER_API_KEY=

# The Control Center Access URL shown under My Account -> Control Center API
# (e.g. https://cloud.gravityzone.bitdefender.com for GravityZone Cloud, or
# your own on-premise Control Center's base URL). This connector targets
# only the JSON-RPC APIs published at <BITDEFENDER_ACCESS_URL>/v1.0/jsonrpc/*.
# Stdio and AUTH_MODE=env read these. The gateway-mode compose service does
# not set them and does not use env_file.
BITDEFENDER_ACCESS_URL=

# stdio (default) or http
# MCP_TRANSPORT=stdio

# gateway: X-Bitdefender-Api-Key and X-Bitdefender-Access-Url on each /mcp
#          request. Never falls back to BITDEFENDER_*. Docker image and
#          Compose default.
# env:     use BITDEFENDER_* after X-Gateway-S2S verifies.
# AUTH_MODE=env

# Required to start the HTTP transport. Leave this empty here.
# The process logs an error and exits non-zero when this is empty or a known
# placeholder (changeme, replace-with-a-real-secret, and similar copied
# examples). Compose will not start when it is unset. Never commit a real value.
# Generate one with: openssl rand -hex 32
CONDUIT_S2S_SECRET=

# Local development only. Set to exactly 1 to start HTTP without
# CONDUIT_S2S_SECRET. Logs a warning, does not enforce X-Gateway-S2S, and
# binds 127.0.0.1 only (a wider MCP_HTTP_HOST is ignored). A known placeholder
# secret is still rejected. Do not use in production.
# MCP_ALLOW_INSECURE_DEV=1

# Bind address for HTTP when CONDUIT_S2S_SECRET is set. Defaults to 127.0.0.1.
# The container image sets 0.0.0.0. Without a secret, the listener is 127.0.0.1.
# MCP_HTTP_HOST=127.0.0.1
# MCP_HTTP_PORT=8080
